sentences.text:
Hence, following order:
a) In the event of arrest of the applicant in connection with C.R. No.238 of 2023 registered with Karveer Police Station, Kolhapur for offence punishable under section 376, 376(2)(n), 354-A, 313, 323, 504, 506 of Indian Penal Code, 1860, he be released on interim bail on furnishing P.R. Bond in the amount of Rs.50,000/-
along with one or two sureties in the like amount;
b) The applicant shall remain present before the investigating officer on 23, 26 and 28 June 2023,
and thereafter as and when called by the concerned investigating officer;
c) The applicant shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any witness acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer;
d) The applicant shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
5. List the anticipatory bail application on 17 July 2023.
(AMIT BORKAR, J.)
Anwar Gafoor Shaikh vs The State Of Maharashtra on 20 June, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/146624487/
